# AI Agent Rules

Agents must have a clearly defined responsibility.

Avoid creating a single general-purpose agent.

Each agent should define:

- input
- output
- tools
- constraints
- failure behavior

Prefer structured outputs over free-form text.

All extracted changes must contain source evidence.

The agent must distinguish:

- documented facts
- inferred information
- uncertainty

The agent must never invent:

- migration instructions
- API behavior
- source URLs
- component usage
- test results

When information is unavailable, explicitly return an uncertainty state.

Prefer tool calls for repository inspection instead of asking an LLM to infer repository state.

Generated code must be treated as a proposal until reviewed by a human.